//// A method called on a number LITERAL. `42.toString()` reached the emitted
//// JavaScript verbatim, and node lexes `42.` as a float — `SyntaxError:
//// Invalid or unexpected token` on the whole module — while erlang and wasm
//// printed `42`. The receiver is spelled `(42).toString()` on commonJS; a
//// bound number (`n.toString()`) never had the defect and is here so the two
//// spellings answer the same thing. Reported by `12-language-tests` (1.0.5-beta
//// front 04's handover section) and carried by C-18.

pub fn main() {
    @print(42.toString());
    val n = 7;
    @print(n.toString());
    @print(3.toString().length());
}
